```

## C8_1_HighestApplies

C-8.1: the higher multiplier governs the payment, but the TOIL accrual under the second sentence of C-5.1 is NOT displaced -- C-7.1 substitutes only for amounts payable under C-4 and C-8.1 speaks only of multipliers. Found by the adversarial reviewer; see tests/counterexamples/CE-0001.yaml.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestC8_1_HighestApplies:
  output r content Overtime.HourPremium

scope TestC8_1_HighestApplies:
  definition r equals
    output of Overtime.HourPremium with {
      -- ordinal: 50
      -- grade: 5
      -- is_public_holiday: true
      -- is_critical_incident: false
      -- is_night: false
      -- has_standing_shift_allowance: false
    }
  assertion r.multiplier = 2.0
  assertion r.salaried_element = 0.0
  assertion r.additional_payable = 2.0
  assertion r.night_premium = 0.0
  assertion r.total_rate = 2.0
  assertion r.accrues_toil = true
```

## C8_1_HolidayAndIncident

C-8.1: C-5.2 gives 1.25 and C-7.1 gives 2.0; the higher governs.

```catala
